  "readmeFile": "docs\\README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.1.1\n- An About button on the toolbar now shows which build you have and where to report what is wrong.\nFull changelog, with screenshots: https://github.com/comentality/xrm-events-2-code/releases/tag/v1.1.1\n\nv1.1.0\n- Changing the connection now clears the old environment from the window, so no write can land in the wrong one.\n- On a slow connection the forms list and handler grid always show what you clicked last, and the buttons wait for it.\n- Loading tables, forms and a form's XML can now be cancelled from the Cancel button on the loading panel.\n- A failed load now stays on the status line, which also says what is still loading instead of counting too early.\n- Closing the tab mid-load no longer pops up an error later, and a save to a dead share no longer freezes the window.\n\nv1.0.0\n- Browse tables and their Main and Quick Create forms over an XrmToolBox connection, with a filter on display or logical name.\n- List every event handler a form registers through the designer, with its event, target, function, library and enabled state.\n- Generate a single OnLoad bootstrap function that registers the checked handlers through the Client API.\n- Designer quirks are preserved: extra parameters and the \"pass execution context\" flag are re-emitted through wrapper closures.\n- Copy the generated code to the clipboard or save it to a .js file.\n- Unregister the checked handlers: they leave the form XML, the bootstrap is registered on form OnLoad, and the table is published.\n- Back up the form XML to Documents\\Events2Code\\backups before any change, and warn on managed forms.\n- The generated-code preview is syntax highlighted.",
